  "question": "If \\(a,b,c,d\\) are real numbers such that \\(b>0,d>0\\) and \\(\\frac ab<\\frac cd\\), then only one of the following statements is always true. Which one is it?",
  "options": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac ab<\\frac{a-c}{b-d}<\\frac cd\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac ab<\\frac{a+c}{b+d}<\\frac cd\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac ab<\\frac{a-c}{b+d}<\\frac cd\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac ab<\\frac{a+c}{b-d}<\\frac cd\\)"
  },
  "answer": "B",
